Source: pycdc commit 25ed1ab2 (pycdc 0.6.0, MIT). See LICENSE for the MIT license.

The rxd copy disables upstream standalone binaries in Cargo.toml; rxd invokes the
library directly. The marshal reader adds depth/object budgets and bounds collection
reservations against input bytes before parsing untrusted input. The source printer and
JSON serializer enforce output budgets before appending beyond the limit. Version
overrides reuse the cached magic table. Nested lambda/annotation/type-parameter
decompilation propagates detected incompleteness to the enclosing result.

Local changes also bound reference-expanded object counts/depth, aggregate marshal byte
copies, quadratic integer conversion work and code-header counts; add strict
instruction/prefix/cache/exception validation; and provide bounded static code/constant/
reference evidence. No analyzed code is executed, and worker isolation is not an OS
sandbox. The imported Rust files are formatted with this workspace's rustfmt version so
`cargo fmt --all -- --check` passes. The upstream library opts out of the workspace Clippy
gate; rxd-pyc and the CLI adapter remain gated.

Upstream attribution and licensing remain unchanged. Any later local change belongs in
this vendored copy and should be documented here. Tests and corpus provenance are in
`tests/corpus/pyc/README.md` and `tests/fixtures/pyc/README.md`.
